# Docker build-context exclusions.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS: Dockerfile:44 is `COPY . /app/` and this repo had no
# .dockerignore, so EVERY file in the tree was shipped into the image --
# .git history, local virtualenvs, caches, editor/agent state, secrets in
# .env files, and abandoned editor backups (*.keycloak_bak, *.auth_fix).
#
# ANYTHING THE BUILD NEEDS MUST NOT APPEAR BELOW. The build reads, in order:
#   pyproject.toml, uv.lock (Dockerfile:36-37), README.md (:38, it is
#   `readme` in pyproject and hatchling resolves it), then the whole tree via
#   `COPY . /app/` (:44) -- src/ (the wheel package), examples/, init_db.sh,
#   scripts/, docker-entrypoint-initdb.d/, .env.example. None of those are
#   excluded here.
# The image does NOT run pytest (no test step in the Dockerfile), so tests/
# is excluded deliberately.

# --- VCS ---
.git/
.gitignore
.gitattributes

# --- Python environments, bytecode and tool caches ---
.venv/
venv/
env/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
*.pyd
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.hypothesis/
.tox/
.coverage
.coverage.*
htmlcov/
coverage.xml

# --- Secrets and local environment (.env.example is KEPT: it is the
#     documented template and is tracked) ---
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx

# --- Runtime bind-mount targets and local data (compose mounts ./certs and
#     ./src at run time; neither mount is affected by this file) ---
certs/
backups/
data/
logs/
*.sqlite
*.db

# --- Abandoned editor/refactor backups (never meant to ship) ---
*.bak
*.backup
*.old
*.orig
*.save
*.swp
*~
*.keycloak_bak*
*.auth_fix

# --- Agent / IDE / OS state ---
.claude/
.worktrees/
.idea/
.vscode/
.DS_Store
.mcp.json

# --- Not needed at runtime ---
tests/
docs/
.github/

# --- JS tooling (Claude Code CLI is installed via npm inside the image;
#     nothing in this repo is a Node project) ---
node_modules/
npm-debug.log
